The Archon is the elite class of the Theurgist (good wizard route). It needs
alignment +30 or higher at level 30. An Archon fights magic with magic: it
holds its turn to break an enemy chant, and wards its allies.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks</ansi>

  30 Counterspell      holds its turn to counter the first enemy chant it sees
                       (cost 20 mana); see below
  35 Twin ward         Arcane Ward also covers a second ally
  40 Mana Shield       allies in the Archon's row take 10% less damage from
                       spells
  45 Sharper counter   Counterspell lands 10 points more often, and a countered
                       caster loses 10% of its mana
  50 Cheaper counter   Counterspell costs 15 mana
  55 Reflection        once a battle, a ward that absorbs a blow returns half of
                       what it took to the attacker
  60 Archon's Aegis    once a battle, when two or more of the company have no
                       ward, the Archon wards every ally at once (costs two
                       wards' mana)

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Counterspell</ansi>

It is automatic: when a foe is chanting a spell at the start of a round and the
Archon has 20 mana (15 from level 50), it holds its turn (it does not swing or cast that round) and
speaks a counter-word. The chance is the hexes' own: 65 in 100 at equal
Mysticism, one more for each point the Archon has over the caster, never under
25 or over 90 (a boss caster, 25 less). A countered caster loses that chant and
starts again on its next turn. A failed counter spends the turn and the mana.
The Archon is told which it was. Turn it off with <ansi fg="command">strategy [who] abilities off</ansi>.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Elite talents</ansi>

Wizard elite talents (levels 35, 45, 55): Deep Reserves (+10% maximum mana),
Focused Will (blows break your chant 25% less often), Spell Edge (+10% spell
damage). See <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help wizard-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help interrupts</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help abilities</ansi>.
